<h3>Challenges Faced and Solutions Applied</h3>
<ul>
<li>Incomparable old models → unified 4-class manifest</li>
<li>Patient/filename leakage → grouped IDs + hash dedupe</li>
<li>Sigmoid+categorical bug in old EfficientNet → softmax</li>
<li>Unfair fine-tune by layer index → match unfreeze fraction</li>
<li>Non-X-ray uploads → rebuilt gate</li>
<li>Train/serve resize skew → align decode</li>
<li>Missing P/R/F1 historically → evaluate.py</li>
<li>Small COVID set → class weights + honest reporting</li>
</ul>

<h3>Historical Single-Disease Work</h3>
<p>Present prior TB/COVID/pneumonia results and TB architecture leaderboard as <strong>prior art within the project</strong>, clearly labelled not comparable to 4-class scores. Pneumonia classification report numbers (92% acc; class-wise P/R/F1) may be quoted as historical.</p>

<h3>Implementation Status</h3>
<p>State what is complete (pipeline, frontend, portable weights bundle if used) and what depends on local training/eval logs. Portable zip includes three .keras weights for demo without retraining.</p>

<h3>Summary of Findings</h3>
<p>Bullet the scientific findings once numbers exist; until then, emphasise methodological findings (fairness controls, gate improvement 21%→77% non-X-ray reject, ensemble UX).</p>

<!-- ===================== CHAPTER 6 ===================== -->
<h2>CHAPTER 6 — FUTURE RECOMMENDATIONS</h2>

<h3>Conclusion</h3>
<p>Reiterate aim achieved: unified 4-class multi-architecture CXR system with ensemble web deployment and honesty-oriented evaluation design. Restate non-diagnostic scope.</p>

<h3>Recommendations</h3>
<ul>
<li>Always report per-class recall for minority diseases</li>
<li>Keep patient-grouped splits in any extension</li>
<li>Do not compare old binary metrics to 4-class metrics</li>
<li>Use leakage probe when merging heterogeneous public sets</li>
</ul>

<h3>Future Enhancements</h3>
<ul>
<li>More COVID data / multi-centre validation</li>
<li>Grad-CAM / explainability overlays</li>
<li>DICOM support and PACS integration</li>
<li>Calibration (temperature scaling) and decision thresholds per class</li>
<li>Active learning / semi-supervised expansion</li>
<li>Mobile/cloud deployment; auth and audit logs</li>
<li>Optional VGG19/backbone expansion under same harness</li>
</ul>

<h3>Summary of Contributions</h3>
<ol>
<li>Unified 4-class CXR benchmark from three public sources with leakage controls</li>
<li>Fair three-architecture training harness (shared head / matched fine-tune fraction)</li>
<li>Evaluation suite with P/R/F1, balanced accuracy, ensemble, leakage probe</li>
<li>Flask multi-model demo with soft voting, agreement display, and measured X-ray gate</li>
<li>Documentation enabling reproducibility (manifest, scripts, status notes)</li>
</ol>

